  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of poor quality of outlook, impacts on privacy and insufficient natural light within the rear bedrooms of Flat A and insufficient provision of private amenity space for Flat B, and the internal layout of the scheme fails to consider appropriate vertical stacking to reduce noise and vibration impacts would result in substandard and inappropriate accommodation incapable of meeting the reasonable needs of future occupiers, contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D3, D4, D5, D6, D8 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010), DMD5, DMD6, DMD8, DMD9, DMD37, and DMD68 of the Enfield Development Management Document (2014), the London Housing Supplementary Planning Guidance (2016) and the London Plan Housing Design Standards LPG 2023.",
    "The development is located in Flood Zones 2 and 3 and is therefore subject to high risk of flooding. The flood depths in this area are considered too great to allow any bedrooms at ground floor level and due to an inadequate Flood Risk Assessment and source control SuDS measures the development fails to demonstrate that the proposed development would both be safe from flooding; will not increase flood risk elsewhere or demonstrate measures to manage the risk of flooding from surface water run-off and follow the drainage hierarchy in the London Plan. This is contrary to guidance in Section 14 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2021); Policies SI 12 and SI 13 of the London Plan (2021); Policy CP28 of the Core Strategy (2010) and Policies DMD59, DMD60 and DMD61 of the Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
